<title>USA: U.S. adj retail sales up 0.6 pct in Dec - Redbook.</title>
<headline>U.S. adj retail sales up 0.6 pct in Dec - Redbook.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. seasonally adjusted retail sales rose 0.6 percent in the four weeks of fiscal December versus November according to the Lynch, Jones &amp; Ryan Inc Redbook Retail Sales Index.</p>
<p>The index rose 5.8 percent compared to the same month a year ago, the report said. Adjusted retail sales rose 6.2 percent in the week ended December 28 compared with the same week a year ago, it said.</p>
<p>((--N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660))</p>
</text>
